    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραίν-εσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>exhortation, address</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				707
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.45
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ποιήσασθαι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				88
			</span></i>: c. gen. pers., <i>advice</i> or <i>counsel given by</i>
			a person, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				51
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, <i>advice given for, of</i>, or
			<i>towards</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ π. τῶν ξυναλλαγῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.59
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ γνώμης παραινέσει</span>
			<i>to recommend</i> an opinion, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.92
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράκλησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
